<!-- UK Market Profile -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">UK's Apparel Market</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">A Post-Brexit Market With Its Own Rulebook</h2>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:640px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">Since leaving the EU, the UK runs its own tariff schedule, product safety marking (UKCA alongside CE), and trader scheme separate from EU rules — brands who assume "EU-ready" documentation automatically covers the UK often find it doesn't. UK buyers, particularly independent labels selling through Depop, ASOS Marketplace, and similar platforms, also tend to order in smaller, more frequent batches than continental European buyers of a similar size.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- UK DCTS & Duty Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
