      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">UK Import FAQ</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is DCTS and how does it benefit my imports?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">The Developing Countries Trading Scheme (DCTS) is the UK's post-Brexit successor to the old GSP/EBA arrangement, effective since June 2023. Under DCTS Enhanced Preferences, most apparel categories from Bangladesh enter the UK with zero customs duty — a benefit the UK has confirmed continues through Bangladesh's November 2026 LDC graduation, covering 98% of Bangladesh's total exports.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What documents do I need to import clothing from Bangladesh to the UK?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Required documents include commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, and DCTS proof of origin (statement on invoice or REX registration). We also provide textile labeling certificates and compliance documentation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How does post-Brexit customs clearance work for Bangladesh imports?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Post-Brexit, Bangladesh-UK trade operates under DCTS. We provide complete documentation including proof of origin to claim duty-free benefits, which stay in place through and past the 2026 LDC graduation. Customs clearance is handled through HMRC with standard import procedures.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you comply with the UK Modern Slavery Act?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We maintain BSCI and SEDEX certifications, conduct regular social compliance audits, and provide supply chain documentation to help UK brands meet their Modern Slavery Act due diligence requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How long does shipping from Bangladesh to the UK take?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Ocean freight to Felixstowe takes 20-25 days, to Southampton 22-27 days. Production adds 30-45 days before shipping. Air freight reduces transit to 5-7 days for urgent orders. Weekly sailings ensure reliable delivery schedules.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do I need separate UK documentation if I already have EU paperwork?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Usually yes. UKCA marking and UK-specific labeling requirements are separate from CE/EU documentation post-Brexit. We prepare UK-compliant paperwork alongside EU documentation for brands shipping to both markets from the same order.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

